Third-party components
------------------------------------------------------------------------

third_party/mbedtls/
    A subset of Arm Mbed TLS (AES, GCM, SHA-256, HKDF and supporting
    glue) is vendored under third_party/mbedtls/. Only the files needed
    by SOFA are included; the upstream tree has been trimmed but the
    retained source files are otherwise unmodified. SOFA's own Mbed TLS
    build configuration lives in shared/mbedtls_fbsec_config.h and is not
    part of upstream.

    Mbed TLS is provided by Arm Limited and contributors under a dual
    Apache-2.0 OR GPL-2.0-or-later license. SOFA takes Mbed TLS under the
    Apache-2.0 option, consistent with SOFA's own license. The full
    upstream license text is preserved at third_party/mbedtls/LICENSE.

    Upstream project: https://github.com/Mbed-TLS/mbedtls

------------------------------------------------------------------------
Optional runtime dependency (not redistributed)
------------------------------------------------------------------------

The CANopen FD bus simulator can optionally bridge to a physical CAN FD
network through PEAK-System's PCANBasic.dll, which it resolves at runtime
via LoadLibrary. PCANBasic.dll is NOT included in this distribution and
is governed by PEAK-System's own license. SOFA builds and runs without
it; only the optional hardware bridge is unavailable when it is absent.
